IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oas-core-periods`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-payment`

-- Old Age Security Act, PART III, sections 23 to 26: when payment of an allowance begins, the Minister's duty to
-- consider an application and give notice, payment in arrears, and which sections of Part II apply to the allowance.
-- Piece oa2.
--
-- The "earlier date, not prior to the day on which the application was received, as may be prescribed by regulation"
-- of section 23(1), and the one of 23(2), are fixed by the Regulations (piece oa3) and enter as inputs named for
-- them; what the section itself fixes (the floor on the earlier date) is encoded.

§ `Part III -- Monthly Allowances`

§§ `Commencement of allowance, section 23`

-- (1) "Payment of an allowance to any person under this Part shall commence in the first month after the application
-- therefor has been approved"
-- src:796 | 23 (1) Payment of an allowance to any person under this Part shall commence in the first month after the application therefor has been approved, but where an application is approved after the last day of the month in which it was received, the approval may be effective as of such earlier date, not prior to the day on which the application was received, as may be prescribed by regulation.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 23(1) first month (src:796)
GIVEN `the day on which the application for the allowance is approved` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 23(1): the first month for which payment of the allowance commences` `the day on which the application for the allowance is approved` MEANS
    `the first day of the month that is` 1 `months after the month containing` `the day on which the application for the allowance is approved`

-- (1) "but where an application is approved after the last day of the month in which it was received, the approval may
-- be effective as of such earlier date, not prior to the day on which the application was received, as may be
-- prescribed by regulation": the date prescribed is an input; it counts only where the approval came after the last
-- day of the month of receipt and the date is not before the day of receipt.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 23(1) "such earlier date" (src:796)
GIVEN `the day on which the application is received` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application for the allowance is approved` IS A DATE
      `the earlier date prescribed by regulation` IS A MAYBE DATE     -- out of range: Regulations s 26.1 and the regulations made under s 23(1) (piece oa3)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 23(1): the earlier date as of which the approval may be effective` `the day on which the application is received` `the day on which the application for the allowance is approved` `the earlier date prescribed by regulation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the earlier date prescribed by regulation`
    WHEN JUST prescribed THEN
        IF     `the day on which the application for the allowance is approved` GREATER THAN `the last day of the month containing` `the day on which the application is received`
           AND prescribed AT LEAST `the day on which the application is received`
        THEN JUST prescribed
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- (1.1) "Where the requirement for an application for payment of an allowance has been waived under this Part, the
-- payment of the allowance shall not commence more than eleven months before the month in which the requirement for
-- an application is waived."
-- src:798 | (1.1) Where the requirement for an application for payment of an allowance has been waived under this Part, the payment of the allowance shall not commence more than eleven months before the month in which the requirement for an application is waived.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 23(1.1) (src:798)
GIVEN `the month in which the requirement for an application is waived` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 23(1.1): the earliest month in which payment of the allowance may commence` `the month in which the requirement for an application is waived` MEANS
    `the first day of the month that is` (0 MINUS 11) `months after the month containing` `the month in which the requirement for an application is waived`

-- (2) "Notwithstanding subsection (1), where a person who has applied to receive an allowance attained the age of sixty
-- years before the day on which the application was received, the approval of the application may be effective as of
-- such earlier day, not before the later of (a) a day one year before the day on which the application was received,
-- and (b) the day on which the person attained the age of sixty years, as may be prescribed by regulation."
-- src:800 | (2) Notwithstanding subsection (1), where a person who has applied to receive an allowance attained the age of sixty years before the day on which the application was received, the approval of the application may be effective as of such earlier day, not before the later of
-- src:801 | (a) a day one year before the day on which the application was received, and
-- src:802 | (b) the day on which the person attained the age of sixty years,
-- src:803 | as may be prescribed by regulation.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 23(2) floor (src:800-803)
GIVEN `the person's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application is received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 23(2): the earliest day to which the approval may be made effective` `the person's date of birth` `the day on which the application is received` MEANS
    IF sixty LESS THAN `the day on which the application is received`
    THEN JUST (IF oneYearBefore GREATER THAN sixty THEN oneYearBefore ELSE sixty)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        sixty MEANS `the day on which a person born on` `the person's date of birth` `attains the age of` 60
        oneYearBefore MEANS `the day that is` (`a limit in years` 1) `before` `the day on which the application is received`

@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 23(2) "as may be prescribed by regulation" (src:803)
GIVEN `the earliest day to which the approval may be made effective` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the earlier day prescribed by regulation` IS A DATE     -- out of range: the regulations made under s 23(2) (piece oa3)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(2): the approval may be effective as of the day prescribed` `the earliest day to which the approval may be made effective` `the earlier day prescribed by regulation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the earliest day to which the approval may be made effective`
    WHEN JUST earliest THEN `the earlier day prescribed by regulation` AT LEAST earliest
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- (3) "Despite subsections (1) and (1.1), if the application for an allowance by a person described in paragraph
-- 19(6)(f) or 21(9)(d) is approved while that person is incarcerated, payment of their allowance shall commence in
-- respect of the month in which they are released but only if they (a) have notified the Minister in writing before or
-- after their release; and (b) continue to be eligible for an allowance."
-- src:805 | (3) Despite subsections (1) and (1.1), if the application for an allowance by a person described in paragraph 19(6)(f) or 21(9)(d) is approved while that person is incarcerated, payment of their allowance shall commence in respect of the month in which they are released but only if they
-- src:806 | (a) have notified the Minister in writing before or after their release; and
-- src:807 | (b) continue to be eligible for an allowance.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 23(3) (src:805-807)
GIVEN `the person is described in paragraph 19(6)(f) or 21(9)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is approved while the person is incarcerated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has notified the Minister in writing before or after the release` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person continues to be eligible for an allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(3): payment of the allowance commences in respect of the month of release` `the person is described in paragraph 19(6)(f) or 21(9)(d)` `the application is approved while the person is incarcerated` `the person has notified the Minister in writing before or after the release` `the person continues to be eligible for an allowance` MEANS
        `the person is described in paragraph 19(6)(f) or 21(9)(d)`
    AND `the application is approved while the person is incarcerated`
    AND `the person has notified the Minister in writing before or after the release`
    AND `the person continues to be eligible for an allowance`

§§ `Payment of allowance, sections 24 and 25`

-- 24(1) "The Minister shall, without delay after receiving an application for an allowance under subsection 19(4) or
-- 21(4) or after waiving the requirement for an application for an allowance under subsection 19(4.1) or 21(5.1), as
-- the case may be, consider whether the applicant is entitled to be paid an allowance, and may approve payment of an
-- allowance and fix the amount of benefits that may be paid, or may determine that no allowance may be paid."
-- src:811 | 24 (1) The Minister shall, without delay after receiving an application for an allowance under subsection 19(4) or 21(4) or after waiving the requirement for an application for an allowance under subsection 19(4.1) or 21(5.1), as the case may be, consider whether the applicant is entitled to be paid an allowance, and may approve payment of an allowance and fix the amount of benefits that may be paid, or may determine that no allowance may be paid.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 24(1) (src:811)
GIVEN `the Minister has received an application for an allowance under subsection 19(4) or 21(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has waived the requirement for an application under subsection 19(4.1) or 21(5.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24(1): the Minister must consider without delay whether the applicant is entitled to be paid an allowance` `the Minister has received an application for an allowance under subsection 19(4) or 21(4)` `the Minister has waived the requirement for an application under subsection 19(4.1) or 21(5.1)` MEANS
    `the Minister has received an application for an allowance under subsection 19(4) or 21(4)` OR `the Minister has waived the requirement for an application under subsection 19(4.1) or 21(5.1)`

-- 24(2) "Where particulars of the basis on which the amount of any allowance that may be paid in respect of an
-- application was fixed by the Minister are requested by an applicant or where the Minister determines that no
-- allowance may be paid in respect of the application, the Minister shall forthwith in writing notify the applicants or
-- applicant of the basis on which that amount was fixed or of the decision that no allowance may be paid in respect of
-- the application and the Minister's reasons therefor, as the case may be."
-- src:813 | (2) Where particulars of the basis on which the amount of any allowance that may be paid in respect of an application was fixed by the Minister are requested by an applicant or where the Minister determines that no allowance may be paid in respect of the application, the Minister shall forthwith in writing notify the applicants or applicant of the basis on which that amount was fixed or of the decision that no allowance may be paid in respect of the application and the Minister’s reasons therefor, as the case may be.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 24(2) basis requested (src:813)
GIVEN `the applicant has requested particulars of the basis on which the amount of the allowance was fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24(2): the Minister must forthwith notify the applicant in writing of the basis on which the amount was fixed` `the applicant has requested particulars of the basis on which the amount of the allowance was fixed` MEANS
    `the applicant has requested particulars of the basis on which the amount of the allowance was fixed`

-- src:813 | (2) Where particulars of the basis on which the amount of any allowance that may be paid in respect of an application was fixed by the Minister are requested by an applicant or where the Minister determines that no allowance may be paid in respect of the application, the Minister shall forthwith in writing notify the applicants or applicant of the basis on which that amount was fixed or of the decision that no allowance may be paid in respect of the application and the Minister’s reasons therefor, as the case may be.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 24(2) no allowance (src:813)
GIVEN `the Minister has determined that no allowance may be paid in respect of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24(2): the Minister must forthwith notify the applicant in writing of the decision that no allowance may be paid and the Minister's reasons` `the Minister has determined that no allowance may be paid in respect of the application` MEANS
    `the Minister has determined that no allowance may be paid in respect of the application`

-- 25 "Payment of an allowance for any month shall be made in arrears at the end of the month, except that where
-- payment of an allowance in respect of any payment period is approved after the end of the month for which the first
-- payment of the allowance may be made, payments thereof for the month in which payment of the allowance is approved
-- and for months preceding that month may be made at the end of that month or at the end of the month next following
-- that month." The same as section 17 for a supplement, and using its record.
-- src:815 | 25 Payment of an allowance for any month shall be made in arrears at the end of the month, except that where payment of an allowance in respect of any payment period is approved after the end of the month for which the first payment of the allowance may be made, payments thereof for the month in which payment of the allowance is approved and for months preceding that month may be made at the end of that month or at the end of the month next following that month.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 25 (src:815)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the month for which the first payment of the allowance may be made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which payment of the allowance is approved` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `s 17: End-of-month days on which payment may be made`
`s 25: the end-of-month days on which payment of the allowance for the month may be made` month `the month for which the first payment of the allowance may be made` `the day on which payment of the allowance is approved` MEANS
    IF     `the day on which payment of the allowance is approved` GREATER THAN `the last day of the month containing` `the month for which the first payment of the allowance may be made`
       AND `the first day of the month containing` month AT MOST `the first day of the month containing` `the day on which payment of the allowance is approved`
    THEN `s 17: End-of-month days on which payment may be made` OF
             (`the last day of the month containing` `the day on which payment of the allowance is approved`),
             (`the last day of the month containing` (`the first day of the month that is` 1 `months after the month containing` `the day on which payment of the allowance is approved`))
    ELSE `s 17: End-of-month days on which payment may be made` OF
             (`the last day of the month containing` month),
             (`the last day of the month containing` month)

§§ `Application of Part II, section 26`

-- 26(1) "Sections 6, 14, 15 and 18 apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, in respect of an
-- allowance under this Part and in respect of any application or any waiver of the requirement for an application for
-- an allowance." The modifications are not stated. This encoding applies the rules of sections 14, 15 and 18 to the
-- allowance by giving them the allowance's facts as inputs, and says here that they apply (fork F-26-1); section 6 is
-- piece oa1's.
-- src:817 | 26 (1) Sections 6, 14, 15 and 18 apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, in respect of an allowance under this Part and in respect of any application or any waiver of the requirement for an application for an allowance.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 26(1) (src:817)
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26(1): sections 14, 15 and 18 apply by virtue of section 26(1) in respect of the benefit` benefit MEANS
    CONSIDER benefit
    WHEN Allowance THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- 26(1.1) "For greater certainty, the Minister may waive the requirements of subsections 14(1) and 15(1) and (2) in
-- respect of an application for an allowance under this Part if the information required under those subsections has
-- already been submitted to or filed with the Minister in respect of an application for a supplement under Part II."
-- src:819 | (1.1) For greater certainty, the Minister may waive the requirements of subsections 14(1) and 15(1) and (2) in respect of an application for an allowance under this Part if the information required under those subsections has already been submitted to or filed with the Minister in respect of an application for a supplement under Part II.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 26(1.1) (src:819)
GIVEN `the information required under subsections 14(1) and 15(1) and (2) has already been submitted to or filed with the Minister in respect of an application for a supplement under Part II` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26(1.1): the Minister may waive the requirements of subsections 14(1) and 15(1) and (2) in respect of an application for an allowance` `the information required under subsections 14(1) and 15(1) and (2) has already been submitted to or filed with the Minister in respect of an application for a supplement under Part II` MEANS
    `the information required under subsections 14(1) and 15(1) and (2) has already been submitted to or filed with the Minister in respect of an application for a supplement under Part II`

-- 26(2) "The provisions of subsection 11(2) and sections 16 to 18 apply, with such modifications as the circumstances
-- require, in respect of the supplement payable to the pensioner pursuant to subsection 22(2)."
-- src:821 | (2) The provisions of subsection 11(2) and sections 16 to 18 apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, in respect of the supplement payable to the pensioner pursuant to subsection 22(2).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 26(2) (src:821)
GIVEN `the supplement is payable to the pensioner pursuant to subsection 22(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26(2): subsection 11(2) and sections 16 to 18 apply in respect of the supplement` `the supplement is payable to the pensioner pursuant to subsection 22(2)` MEANS
    `the supplement is payable to the pensioner pursuant to subsection 22(2)`
